\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There's a light upon the mountains, 
\par and the day is at the spring.
\par When our eyes shall see the beauty 
\par and the glory of the king
\par Weary was our heart with waiting, 
\par and the night-watch seemed so long ;
\par But  His triumph-day is breaking, 
\par and we hail it with a song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In the fading of the straight 
\par we can see the coming morn ;
\par And the lights of the men are palling 
\par in the splendours of the dawn  ;
\par For the eastern skies are glowing 
\par as with light of hidden fire,
\par And the hearts of men are stirring
\par with the throbs of deep desire.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There's a hush of expectation, 
\par and a quiet in the air ;
\par And the breath of God is moving 
\par in the fervent breath of prayer :
\par For the suffering, dying Jesus 
\par is the Christ  upon the throne,
\par And the travail of our spirit 
\par is the travail of His own .
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He is breaking down the barriers, 
\par He is casting up the way ;
\par He is calling for His angels to build up 
\par the gates of day ;
\par But His angels here are human, 
\par not the shining hosts above ;
\par For the drum-beats of His army  
\par are  the heart-beat of our love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hark ! we hear a distant music, 
\par and it comes with fuller swell ;
\par ' Tis  the triumph-song of Jesus, 
\par of our King, Immanuel :
\par Zion, go ye forth to meet Him ; 
\par and, my soul, be swift to bring
\par All thy sweetest and thy dearest 
\par for the triumph of our King !  
\par \i 
\par \i0\f1 
